@startuml
title ioScope Quality Attribute Tactics - Overview

skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 10
}
skinparam shadowing false
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Availability\nio_scope_quality_attribute_availability.puml\n--\nhealth monitoring and supervised recovery" as availability
rectangle "Performance\nio_scope_quality_attribute_performance.puml\n--\nthreaded pipeline and bounded buffering" as performance
rectangle "Usability\nio_scope_quality_attribute_usability.puml\n--\npresets, saved settings, inline feedback" as usability
rectangle "Security\nio_scope_quality_attribute_security.puml\n--\nauthentication, authorization, auditing" as security
rectangle "Safety\nio_scope_quality_attribute_safety.puml\n--\nsafe limits, validation, remote interlock" as safety
rectangle "Energy Efficiency\nio_scope_quality_attribute_energy_efficiency.puml\n--\nidle detection, sleep mode, fast wake" as energy

availability -[hidden]-> performance
performance -[hidden]-> usability
usability -[hidden]-> security
security -[hidden]-> safety
safety -[hidden]-> energy

note bottom
Each quality attribute now has its own structural diagram.
This overview exists only as a small index for the split set.
Implemented and proposed classes are marked inside the
individual quality-attribute files.
end note

@enduml
